NAME
       kill, sigaction, sigprocmask - signals

SYNOPSIS
       #include <signal.h>

       int kill(pid_t pid, int sig);
       int sigaction(int sig, const struct sigaction *act,
                     struct sigaction *old);
       int sigprocmask(int how, const sigset_t *set, sigset_t *old);

DESCRIPTION
       Cervus implements real signals. Delivery builds a frame on the
       user stack and returns through the __sigtramp stub in libc,
       which calls sigreturn.

       A blocking terminal read is interrupted by a signal and fails
       with EINTR rather than swallowing it.

       Ctrl-C sends SIGINT to the whole foreground process group, so a
       script dies together with the command it is running. A console
       font change sends SIGWINCH to the foreground subtree.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ESRCH    no such process
       EINVAL   the signal number is not valid
       EPERM    not permitted to signal that process

SEE ALSO
       kill(1), sigtest(1), poll(2)
